  "gloss": "lamentation; deploring",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "lamentation; deploring; grieving over",
      "explanation": "A literary word for grieving over and deploring something one finds deeply regrettable, such as social decline or injustice. More formal than {嘆|なげ}く."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29741_gaitan_ex1",
      "japanese": "{現状|げんじょう}を{慨嘆|がいたん}する。",
      "english": "to lament the current situation.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29741_gaitan_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{世|よ}の{乱|みだ}れを{慨嘆|がいたん}した。",
      "english": "He deplored the disorder of the world.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29741_gaitan_ex3",
      "japanese": "{老人|ろうじん}は{若者|わかもの}の{礼儀|れいぎ}のなさを{慨嘆|がいたん}した。",
      "english": "The old man lamented the lack of manners among young people.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A formal, somewhat literary word for grieving over and deploring something regrettable, such as social decline or injustice. Combines sorrow with a note of indignation.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {世相|せそう}を{慨嘆|がいたん}する: to lament the state of society\n- {慨嘆|がいたん}の{声|こえ}: voices of lamentation\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {嘆|なげ}く: to grieve, lament — everyday word, broader\n- {憤慨|ふんがい}: indignation — emphasizes anger rather than sorrow",
